  "result": {
    "brief": "ned to GPU 1, all inference serialized behind one lock, no storage side effects (`services/wraith-infer/server.py:1-22, :44-56, :71-78`; `services/wraith-infer/run.sh:17, :35`).\n\n**Local services are DOWN.** `curl -m4 localhost:{8000/health, 8001/api/v1/heartbeat, 8100/health}` → empty; `ps aux | grep -iE 'chroma|api_embedder|vllm|uvicorn|wraith'` → no matches; `ss -ltnp | grep -E ':8000|:8001|:8002|:8100|:3847'` → empty. `.run/chroma.pid` 5972, `.run/embedder.pid` 6008, `.run/marker.pid` 6555 are **stale**.\n\n**Retrieval already wired to the reranker** (§4.3): `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:240` (rerank call), `:901` (`kind:'query'`), `:931` (poolSize), `:1184-1197` (enable + endpoint default), `:1206` (candidateMultiplier), `:1210-1220` (rerankResults); `config-manager.ts:134-138, :284-285, :365-366` carries `services.rerank` + `GOD_RERANK_ENDPOINT` / `GOD_RERANK_ENABLED`.\n\n**Chroma is chunk-level, not entry-level:** `god_agent_vectors_1536` 413,160 · `local_vectors_1536` 153,919 · `knowledge_chunks` 11,858 · `dissertation-perplexity-cache` 2,599 · `v2_knowledge_chunks` 167 (6.5 GB total).\n\n**Ontology-embedding precedent (stale):** `tmp/analysis-upgrade/production-sandbox/data/corpus/index/ontology-embeddings.v1.jsonl` 9.57 MB, 2026-04-19, **278 records** `{name, greek, embedding[1536]}` covering **277/701 = 39.5%** of the live ontology. Reusable pipeline: `embed_ontology.py:11-13, :22-30` (concatenates `name + greek + transliteration + translation + definition[:600]`, POSTs batches of 16 to `localhost:8000/embed`); `resolve_concepts.py:10-12` (top-K=5 cosine, `MIN_SCORE=0.55`). It produced 557 concept-mentions from 119 claims and 24 LLM-judged bridge candidates (4 substantive) (`tmp/analysis-upgrade/04-final-summary.md:58-70`).\n\n**Eval verdict on the retrieval stack** (memory `project-wraith-retrieval-upgrade.md:21`): on a 15-query gold set, raw 1536 gte-Qwen2 is a **REGRESSION** vs 768 fastembed (MRR 0.285 vs 0.493); the **cross-encoder reranker is the win** — 768+rerank best MRR 0.547, 1536+rerank best recall R@10 0.573. Decision: keep both; archon stays fastembed-768 default; reranker + 1536 opt-in. **⇒ any grouping query should be embed-recall → rerank-precision, not pure cosine.**\n\n**The only existing \"group query\" is string-matching, not semantic:** `cross-author-utils.ts:440-474` / `:500-530` — drop words <5 chars, lowercase, substring containment against hook `sourceConcept`/`targetConcept` and tension `nodeA`/`nodeB`/`description`, hard cap 1 bridge per facet.\n\n### 9.3 Hard problems (blockers, in dependency order)\n\n| # | Problem | Evidence | Blocks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **G-1** | **The gold-standard cluster is invisible to the only cross-entry substrate.** 8 of 27 entries are unregistered (§3.4), including Phantasia Secondary, Emotion Secondary, both RDR2 entries, Game-Behavior Method, Motion&Time, Veri(dis)similitude, Dissertation | verified set-diff | Any grouping built on `compiled-index.json` silently omits precisely the material the example query is about |\n| **G-2** | **Registering them is a FORMAT rewrite, not a config edit.** None of the three \"parseable\" candidates is parseable: `grep -cE '^#### [0-9]+\\.'` and `grep -cE '^\\|'` → Phantasia hdr=0 tbl=0 · RDR2 Secondary hdr=0 tbl=0 · Emotion Secondary hdr=0 tbl=0. Their H2s are prose section names (`## Volume-pillar concepts (Tier-1)`, `## Canonical CONCEPT nodes (38)`, `## Organizing structure`) with no `## 3A`. Body form: `corpus/index/Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary (1985-2017)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.md:9` → `**PHX-C-001 phantasia (the faculty/phenomenon)** is the unavoidable umbrella…`. Registered exemplar for contrast: Boredom Secondary hdr=**68** | verified greps | G-1 |\n| **G-3** | **Four incompatible per-unit JSON schemas + four incompatible `global-edges.csv` layouts + four `concept-matrix.csv` orientations. No shared unit-record type, no schema file, no validator.** `loci` in 2/17 entries, `greek_terms` in 3/17, `bridges` in 2/17 | §2.2, §2.4, §2.5 | Structured-field similarity is impossible without a normalization adapter per schema family; any signal restricted to `loci` or `greek_terms` covers 2–3 entries only |\n| **G-4** | **\"Common artifact set\" is a naming convention, not an interface.** cluster-ontology.json 5 schemas · debate-map.json 5 · citation-network.json 5 · book-level-ontology.json 7 · tension-edges.json 10 · concept-matrix.csv 16 headers. Relation vocabularies are cluster-disjoint at the head | §2.6 | Nothing can consume the five clusters uniformly today |\n| **G-5** | **Granularity mismatch across every available signal.** Request = groups of ENTRIES; ontology embeddings = per-CONCEPT-NODE (701, of which 278 embedded); Chroma = per-CHUNK (413k); folders = per-DOCUMENT (269 unit JSONs); manifests = per-CLUSTER (5). **Nothing is embedded at the unit or entry level** | §9.2 | Any grouping architecture must first choose and construct a representation level |\n| **G-6** | **No programmatic producer for any synthesis artifact** (§8.5) | grep | \"Auto-generate a group\" = orchestrating an LLM pipeline over retrieved evidence, not a deterministic transform. Only member-selection and evidence-assembly can be pure code |\n| **G-7** | **Ontology-node parse pollution** — `centralityTier` and `type` contain dumped markdown tables and malformed composites (C-1). Node text used for embedding (`name+greek+translation+definition`) may inherit garbage | §3.6 C-1 | A few nodes produce pathological embedding inputs; `centralityTier`/`type` are unusable as filter keys |\n| **G-8** | **Embeddings stale and the embedder they were made against is down**; and **no eval harness exists** — `corpus/eval/` does not exist, `scripts/eval-retrieval.ts` was never written (Phase 5 of `plans/wraith-retrieval-upgrade-plan-2026-07-17.md:314-320`) | §9.2 | Group-membership precision/recall cannot be measured today |\n\n### 9.4 Candidate architectures (as implied by the evidence; none built)\n\n**A. Compiled-index-only (cheapest, currently broken).** Query `compiled-index.json` ontologyNodes by term + `units[]` back-pointers. **Requires G-1 + G-2 first** (8 entries invisible, 3 of them need an ontology-format rewrite). Also inherits G-7. Coverage today: 10 nodes for \"phantasia\" vs 18 entries with raw hits.\n\n**B. Direct-from-source with per-shape adapters.** Read `_synthesis/` and per-unit JSON off disk, bypassing the compiler entirely — the approach `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md:14-17` already mandates (\"import from SOURCE files, not compiled-index.json\") with its 8 named adapter families (`:45-58`). **Requires G-3/G-4 normalization**; `scripts/normalize-edges.py` exists for exactly this but is hardcoded to 5 pipeline paths (`:37-41`) covering **none** of the five secondary clusters.\n\n**C. Embed-recall → rerank-precision at a constructed representation level.** Re-embed all 701 ontology nodes (and/or construct per-unit documents) via wraith-infer `:8100` with `kind:'document'`; retrieve top-K by cosine; re-rank with `bge-reranker-v2-m3`. Justified by the recorded eval verdict (§9.2) that raw 1536 cosine regresses but rerank wins. Reuses `embed_ontology.py` / `resolve_concepts.py` verbatim. **Requires G-5 decision + G-8 re-embed** (~4 s at the 2026-04 measured rate for 701 nodes).\n\n**D. LLM synthesis over assembled evidence (the actual \"group generator\").** Deterministic pre-pass (member selection via A/B/C + evidence assembly) → LLM authoring of the 12-artifact common core, gated by the numeric quality gates already specified in `TEMPLATE:216-229` and the per-graph node/edge caps already specified in `render-validation.txt`. Cost profile is the entry-creation profile (§8.6), not a transform profile.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Conflicts and risks (architecture-coherence lens)\n\nThe four stated directions were: **(a)** move the index out of `corpus/`, **(b)** mirror corpus organization, **(c)** auto-create a per-document entry on ingest, **(d)** on-demand cross-cutting groups.\n\n**Verdict:** (b) is **not well-defined as stated** — source→domain is a many-to-many relation, not a function. (c) has **no viable quality floor** — ~60% of the value in existing entries is definitionally cross-document. (a) and (d) are feasible; (a) has a 5,500-occurrence prose blast radius and (d) is blocked on G-1/G-2.\n\n### 10.1 Entry-per-document vs cluster conflict\n\nEvery numeric quality gate in the canonical protocol is **cross-unit by construction** (`plans/secondary-cluster-index-plan-TEMPLATE-2026-07-15.md:216-229`): ≥12·N edges · 8–12 debates · 8–12 contested readings · ≥50 lemmas · ≥max(10, N/4) intra-cluster citations · every unit in ≥1 concordance cell. A per-document entry has N=1: debates, contested readings, intra-cluster citations, the concordance grid, the secondary-literature network, the citation network, and the scholarly-evolution arc **all collapse to nothing**. Confirmed by the gold standard's own numbers (§9.2): 32/41 concepts multi-unit; all 12 debates multi-unit; 288 canonical loci canonicalized from 628 raw; 213 lemmas from 279 raw; 31 directed intra-cluster citations.\n\nAuto-creation on ingest would also spawn entries for literature deliberately never indexed — **AD(H)D alone = 17 new entries** (§10.2).\n\n### 10.2 Corpus-domain mapping reality\n\n**Coverage.** Exact-basename provenance resolution over all 288 corpus PDFs against every entry's full text: only **168/288 (58%)** are referenced by any entry.\n\n| Domain | PDFs | Covered |\n|---|---|---|\n| boredom | 50 | 50 |\n| pedagogy | 35 | 35 |\n| download | 35 | 34 |\n| biomedical_engineering | 19 | 19 |\n| rhetorical_ontology | 63 | **24** |\n| new_media | 43 | **2** |\n| metaphysics | 19 | **2** |\n| Virtual Learning Environments | 5 | 1 |\n| Part_II | 1 | 1 |\n| **AD(H)D** | **17** | **0** |\n| **textual_analysis** | **1** | **0** |\n| **dissertation** | 0 files | — |\n\n**Fan-out is 11:1, not 1:1.** `corpus/rhetorical_ontology` (63 PDFs) is the exact-verified source for **eleven** separate curated entries: A Grammar of Motives, A Rhetoric of Motives, Aristotelian Emotion Secondary, Aristotle - Complete Works, Dissertation, Heidegger - BCAP, Heidegger - Being and Time, Heidegger and Rhetoric, Rickert - Ambient Rhetoric, Uncomfortable Situations, Von Uexküll. Mirroring `corpus/` collapses all eleven into one flat directory and destroys the only structure distinguishing \"Aristotle primary\" from \"Phantasia secondary scholarship about Aristotle\" — both of which live in `rhetorical_ontology`.\n\n**Multi-domain entries (exact match, not inference):** Aristotelian Emotion Secondary = `{download, rhetorical_ontology}` (`_synthesis/manifest.json:19-89`; units 01–04 from rhetorical_ontology, `aes-05` supplement from `corpus/download/Jamie_Dow_2011_….pdf`) · Aristotle - Complete Works = `{metaphysics, rhetorical_ontology}` · Boredom Secondary = `{boredom, biomedical_engineering}` · Dissertation = `{download, rhetorical_ontology}`.\n\n**Documents referenced by MORE THAN ONE entry:** `corpus/rhetorical_ontology/Burke, Kenneth - A Rhetoric of Motives_(1950)_[My Copy].pdf` → `{A Grammar of Motives, A Rhetoric of Motives, Dissertation}` (3 PDFs total in this class). **A per-document mirror cannot represent a document that legitimately belongs to two analyses.**\n\n**Cross-domain byte-identical duplicates.** `md5sum` over all 288 corpus PDFs → **23 duplicate hash groups, 20 of them cross-domain**: 17 × `(biomedical_engineering, boredom)`, 2 × `(metaphysics, new_media)` (Heim *The Metaphysics of Virtual Reality*, Heim *Virtual Realism*), 1 × `(download, rhetorical_ontology)` (Corcilius, *Aristotle's Model of Animal Motion*). Boredom Secondary's `units[].sourceFile` values are **bare filenames**, so **17 of its 55 units have genuinely ambiguous domain provenance**.\n\n**Nine entries have no machine-readable source path at all** (§2.11) — their mirror location is undecidable without re-derivation.\n\n**One broken declared path:** `corpus/index/Virtual Learning Environments (King–Salvo)/units/vle-05-scalable-vr-global-immersion.md:3` declares `corpus/virtual_learning_environments/King, Christine and Dalton Salvo - scalable-virtual-reality-….pdf`; `ls -d corpus/virtual_learning_environments` → No such file (actual dir is `corpus/Virtual Learning Environments`, capitalized).\n\n**Consequence:** requirement (b) needs, before it is even specifiable: (i) a canonical-domain rule for the 20 cross-domain duplicates, (ii) a representation for one-document-to-many-entries, (iii) a policy for the 11:1 fan-out, (iv) a decision on the 3 zero-coverage domains, (v) re-derivation of provenance for the 9 entries that declare none.\n\n### 10.3 Quality floor\n\n- The verbatim-quote detector — the mandatory G1 copyright gate — **does not exist** (§8.5). Currently satisfied by agent self-attestation.\n- Mermaid render validation **has never actually been performed** (`mmdc` not installed; RDR2 quality-gates report records it as deferred).\n- Only **2 of 27** entries have a `quality-gates-report.md`; only **1 of 27** (RDR2) has a machine-readable `metrics` object.\n- The compiler has **no self-check** against manifest-declared counts (C-8) and **cannot fail a build** (no `--check`, no non-zero exit).\n- A clean compiler run **proves nothing** — 7 silent-skip sites (§3.5) make malformed input indistinguishable from absent input.\n- `ig-10-incorporation.json` (45,350 B) is **malformed JSON and unparseable** — the only unparseable file of 494 (re-verified this brief): `Expecting ',' delimiter: line 155 column 3 (char 25049)`. Its folder also holds a parallel `ig-10-deep.{json,md,-edges.csv}` triplet, so **which file is authoritative for In-Game chapter 10 is undetermined**.\n\n### 10.4 Key-stability risks\n\n| Risk | Mechanism | Path:line |\n|---|---|---|\n| **doc_id is path-derived** | `doc_id = sha256(f'{path_rel}:{sha256_file}')[:16]`; chunk ids `{doc_id}:{idx:05d}`. Relocating or re-rooting any document mints an entirely new doc_id and chunk-id namespace, with **no dedup against the old chunks** (cleanup is per-doc_id only) | `run_ingest_phase2.py:220-222`, `:659`, `:699`, `:1825-1833` |\n| **Author resolution parses the display label** | `deriveAuthor` splits on `' - '`; the result becomes the ChromaDB `author_raw` exact-match filter for ICP Stage 6b bridge enforcement. Renaming an entry label breaks author-scoped retrieval | `cross-author-utils.ts:364-406`, esp. `:395-398`, `:358-362` |\n| **`text` is a label, not a path, and does not round-trip** | `'Burke - A Grammar of Motives'` ≠ dir `A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)`; 10 Aristotle work-labels are not directories at all; multi-source nodes join with `'; '` | `compile-corpus-index.py:34-147`, `:1330-1332` |\n| **Entry-directory names hardcoded in code** | 5 literal `corpus/index/<Entry Name>/…/global-edges.csv` paths | `scripts/normalize-edges.py:37-41` |\n| **TEXT_DIRS keys are directory names** | Any rename silently drops the entry from the compiled index with no warning | `compile-corpus-index.py:35-133` |\n| **ID prefixes are the only cross-file join key** and are unenforced | 31 prefixes, no registry file; 4 entries use non-numeric schemes; Aristotle mixes uppercase `unit_id` with lowercase filenames | §2.9 |\n| **Nondeterministic compiled artifact** | Every recompile dirties the git-tracked file with meaningless `canonicalTerms` reordering, defeating content-hash staleness checks and making real diffs unreadable | C-2 |\n| **Registration policy already reversed once** | Memory `project-compiled-index-registration.md` says secondary clusters are \"NOT registered, by design\"; Boredom Secondary (61 nodes) and VR Pedagogy (60) are now the **two largest** contributors, enabled by the `cluster-ontology.md` fallback | `compile-corpus-index.py:1217-1224` |\n| **82% of the index has no git history** | 335 of 1,848 files tracked; a `git clean -fd` or fresh clone loses Aristotle (131 files), Dissertation (358), Burke, Heidegger, Calleja, RDR2, Rickert, Uexküll | §6.H |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Corrections (verifier refutations, stated plainly)\n\n### 11.A Re-verified by this brief\n\n| # | Claim | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | \"NINE of 28 entry directories are not in TEXT_DIRS\" (compiler agent) | **WRONG. 8 of 27.** `ls -1 corpus/index` = 28 lines = 27 dirs + `compiled-index.json`; `find -maxdepth 1 -type d` = 28 = 27 entries + `.backups`. TEXT_DIRS = 19. Unregistered = exactly the 8 listed in §3.4. Registered-but-missing = **0**. The entry-creation agent's \"8\" was right; the two agents disagreed and were treated as corroborating |\n| A2 | \"27 entry folders in the hardcoded TEXT_DIRS registry\" (drafting agent) | **WRONG.** TEXT_DIRS has **19** keys. 27 is the on-disk entry count |\n| A3 | Edge-CSV file counts: 219 (anatomy) vs 248 (compiler) vs \"~240\" (entry-creation) | **Canonical: 250 total, 219 excluding `.backups`.** The 219 / 19,770-row / 42-header census is the correct basis |\n| A4 | `tension-edges.json` count: 10 (anatomy) vs 11 (compiler) | **11** (none in `.backups`). The anatomy agent enumerated 10 shapes; the 11th file's shape is **UNVERIFIED** |\n| A5 | Total file count: 1,848 (anatomy, ingestion) vs 1,842 (compiler) | **1,848 total; 1,759 excluding `.backups`.** The compiler agent's 1,842 does not reconcile with either basis (off by 83 from the excl-backups count) |\n| A6 | JSON parseability: \"1 of 404 unparseable\" (anatomy) | **CONFIRMED, count basis differs.** 494 `.json` files excluding `.backups`; exactly **1** unparseable: `corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/Calleja - From Immersion to Incorporation/ig-10-incorporation.json`, `Expecting ',' delimiter: line 155 column 3 (char 25049)` |\n| A7 | compiled-index counts | **CONFIRMED**: 701 / 72 / 64 / 1,722, builtAt `2026-07-20T16:03:58.499584+00:00` |\n| A8 | Anatomy's final gap, truncated at \"8 entry directories are absent fro…\" | **[recovered]** — it is the unregistered-entries gap; the 8 names are in §3.4 |\n\n### 11.B Sandbox-completion skeptic\n\n| # | Refuted claim | Correction |\n|---|---|---|\n| **B1** | \"MASTER-PLAN Phase 0 IS DONE but **FAILED its own gate**\" | **Not a failure — a documented gate substitution.** `backups/pre-promotion-20260419-074829/MANIFEST.md:36-44`: \"All completeness checks PASS: TS consumers: expected 9, found 9; corpus/index/: files 306/306, bytes 6,072,017/6,072,017 (exact match); tmp/analysis-upgrade/: files 133/133, bytes 33,724,440/33,724,440 (exact match)\" … \"### Note on plan gate — MASTER-PLAN phase 0 gate called for '≥1.1GB backed up (the prior sandbox alone is ~900MB)'. Actual measured size … is 33MB (not 900MB) … The plan's size estimate was inaccurate; authoritative gate is 'file count + total size match source', which PASSES exactly. Gate satisfied by exact byte-match verification above, not by size threshold.\" **Phase 0 = COMPLETE.** The real limitation (snapshot at 07:48, production-sandbox created 07:51 ⇒ contains no Phase 2/3a/3b/4 output) stands, but that is scope, not gate failure |\n| **B2** | \"GEN-4 extracted **4,939** claims\" + the per-paper table | **4,961.** All counts came from `wc -l`, but **22 of 24** `claims.jsonl` files have no trailing newline (`tail -c1 … \\| xxd -p` → `7d`), so each is undercounted by exactly one. python non-empty-line count = 4,961. **Downstream consequence: compiled-index.v2.json holds 4,921 claims ⇒ 40 records dropped by the faithfulness filter, not 18.** The same off-by-one affects GEN-1 (119/557/24) and GEN-3 (79/320/24) wherever `wc -l` was used |\n| **B3** | \"ontology-embeddings.jsonl … **277** lines × 1536-D\" / the artifact is \"invalidated\" | **278 records** (same missing-newline artifact; `wc -l` = 277, distinct `name` fields = 278). **277 of them are present in the live 701-node ontology ⇒ 39.5% coverage.** Not invalidated — a valid subset. Re-embedding the 423 newer nodes makes it usable; a from-scratch rebuild is not required |\n| **B4** | Implied: the entire 583 MB sandbox, code included, is at risk from `rm -rf tmp/` | **Split the risk.** The Phase-2/R1/R1.3 **code is committed** as three real commits on `writing-pipeline-v3` (`1268adbcf`, `670fd2939`, `1e0aa7e34`); the branch ref and objects live in the main repo's `.git`, not in `tmp/`. Deleting `tmp/analysis-upgrade` orphans the worktree registration but does not destroy code. **The ~$25 of extracted claim data and ~40 h of gold annotation under `production-sandbox/data/` ARE untracked and irrecoverable — genuinely critical.** The code's real exposure is different and unmentioned: `git ls-remote --heads origin` lists only `writing-pipeline-v2`; `git rev-parse writing-pipeline-v3@{upstream}` → \"no upstream configured\"; tag `pre-promotion-20260419` absent from `git ls-remote --tags origin`. **The code survives tmp-deletion but not disk loss** |\n\n*Note:* the skeptic **confirmed** zero promotion, unchanged caps, absent ACTIVE-CLAIMS wiring, the exact drift numbers, the single merge conflict, the non-fork status of the sandbox compiler, Phase-5-never-ran, Phase-4-partial + governance metastasis, the gold-set decoupling percentages, the GEN-4 artifact inventory, and the untracked/not-gitignored status — all reproduced independently.\n\n### 11.C Architecture-coherence skeptic\n\n| # | Refuted claim | Correction |\n|---|---|---|\n| **C1** | (see A1) \"NINE of 28 not in TEXT_DIRS\" | 8 of 27 |\n| **C2** | \"THREE unregistered entries ship a **real, parseable** `_synthesis/cluster-ontology.md` that is never read … registration is a silent, human-memory-dependent step\" (severity: critical) | **None of the three is parseable.** Phantasia, RDR2 Secondary, and Emotion Secondary all use flowing prose with bold inline IDs — `grep -cE '^#### [0-9]+\\.'` = 0 and `grep -cE '^\\|'` = 0 for all three; no `## 3A` heading in any of them. Adding them to TEXT_DIRS today compiles **zero** nodes and emits **no warning** (`parse_ontology_md` returns an empty list rather than erroring). **The gap is a FORMAT gap, not a wiring gap** — three of the highest-quality clusters, including the nominated gold standard, are written in an ontology dialect no code in the repo can read. Any plan assuming \"register the missing entries\" is a config edit is wrong by roughly one full rewrite per entry |\n| **C3** | \"Provenance … EVERY recorded path resolves on disk\" (anatomy); entry→domain presented as a clean function | **Two errors.** (i) The check was scoped to manifest JSON and missed source declarations in unit `.md` files — `corpus/index/Virtual Learning Environments (King–Salvo)/units/vle-05-scalable-vr-global-immersion.md:3` declares a non-existent `corpus/virtual_learning_environments/` (actual: `corpus/Virtual Learning Environments`). (ii) Boredom Secondary's `units[].sourceFile` values are **bare filenames**, and 17 of 55 resolve in **two** domains because `corpus/biomedical_engineering` holds byte-identical copies of 17 `corpus/boredom` PDFs. **Document→domain is many-to-many** (20 cross-domain duplicate groups total) |\n| **C4** | \"≥10 edges-CSV header dialects (verified)\" (`plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md:60-61`) | **Undercount.** The skeptic counted 20+ distinct headers; the anatomy agent's higher-resolution census over 219 non-backup files found **42**. Canonical `source,relation,target,locus,note` covers only 135 (+5 whitespace variant). *(The 20+ vs 42 delta is unreconciled — likely whitespace/casing variants; one `head -1 \\| sort \\| uniq -c` run on a single fixed basis would settle it. **UNVERIFIED**)* |\n| **C5** | \"A reusable executable spec already exists … 12 artifacts common to all 5 clusters\" ⇒ the shape is reusable (grouping agent) | **True at the FILENAME level, false at the SCHEMA level** — by the grouping agent's own facts (cluster-ontology.json 5 schemas, debate-map.json 5, citation-network.json 5, concept-matrix.csv 4 orientations, global-edges.csv 4 layouts). Independently reconfirmed on `global-edges.csv`: Phantasia 10 cols / 706 rows vs Boredom Secondary 6 cols / 1,897 rows, with disjoint head relation vocabularies. **\"Common artifact set\" is a naming convention, not an interface.** A normalization layer must precede any grouping work |\n\n### 11.D Blast-radius skeptic\n\n| # | Refuted claim | Correction |\n|---|---|---|\n| **D1** | \"Blast radius for relocating corpus/index is small in code (7 files, ~12 lines)\" | **Incomplete — the search was scoped to the literal token `corpus/index`.** A second, string-free coupling class exists: code that reconstructs a corpus path by joining the corpus root to a manifest `path_rel`, and 772 manifest rows begin `index/`. Those sites resolve into `corpus/index` without containing the substring and survive any grep-driven migration. **At least 4 additional MUST-CHANGE sites:** `endnote-generator.ts:31`, `missing_link_detector.py:439`, `coverage_analyzer.py:470`, `orphan_identifier.py:335` (§6.B). **Any migration must also rewrite the 772 manifest `path_rel` values**, or these silently resolve to non-existent files |\n| **D2** | \"There is NO `god ingest` TypeScript CLI\" and \"watch_corpus.py's automation chain is Phase 1 → Phase 2 and nothing else\"; only 2 full-corpus drivers cited | **A third driver was missed, and it is the primary user-facing one.** `scripts/god_learn/god_learn.py:755` defaults `--root` to `<repo>/corpus`; `:332-340` shells `run_ingest_phase2.py --root <root>` → `audit_ingest.py` → `verify_ingest.py`; same pair at `:720-721`. Exposed as `/god-learn-compile` (`.claude/commands/god-learn-compile.md:7`), `/god-learn-update`, `/god-learn-verify`. **One keystroke walks `corpus/index`.** Note it calls Phase 2 ONLY — never Phase 1 |\n| **D3** | \"No runtime data store embeds corpus/index path strings … the ONLY data file carrying those paths is manifest.jsonl\" | **The SQLite vector store was never inspected as a text store.** `strings vector_db_1536/chroma.sqlite3 \\| grep -c corpus/index` = **458**. SQL on a read-only copy: `chroma:document` **41**, `path_abs` **25**, `raw_content` **1**; by collection: `god_agent_vectors_1536 / chroma:document` **39** (embedded prompt/memory text — **not fixable by re-ingestion**), `knowledge_chunks / chroma:document` 2, `/ path_abs` 25, `/ raw_content` 1 |\n| **D4** | Prose blast radius = \"50 plans, 389 tmp files\" + a short docs list; IGNORE list covers the rest | **Two surfaces absent.** (i) `reports/` never mentioned — 3 files (§6.E). (ii) **`corpus/index` is massively self-referential: 297 files inside it (245 `.md`, 51 `.json`, 1 `.mmd`, excluding `.backups`) cite their own location.** That is the dominant term and neither mapping agent counted it. Also `corpus/download/_basic-ingest-summary.md`. Plans split: **47 live** + 2 under `plans/.backups` |\n| **D5** | \".backups ingestion exposure — severity HIGH\", citing `reingest-max.sh` | **Wrong driver.** `reingest-max.sh:55-56` runs `--pdf-only`, and `find corpus/index -path '*/.backups/*' \\( -name '*.md' -o -name '*.pdf' -o -name '*.txt' \\)` → **12 files: 12 md, 0 pdf, 0 txt**. Exposure under that driver is **nil**. Real exposure exists only for the all-extension drivers (`watch_corpus.py`, `god-learn compile` — the latter missed entirely) and is bounded at 12 markdown files. **Downgrade to medium-low and re-attribute** |\n| **D6** | `verify_ingest.py` / `audit_ingest.py` characterized as read-only utilities \"sharing the ingestion walk semantics\" | **They do not share the walk semantics and carry an unflagged portability defect.** No `SKIP_DIRS` at all (`audit_ingest.py:60`, `verify_ingest.py:67`) — they walk `.extracted_media` and `.backups` that the ingesters skip — and both default `--root` to a machine-specific **absolute** path `/home/dalton/projects/claudeflow-testing/corpus` (`:97` / `:166`). **Both are additional MUST-CHANGE sites** |\n\n*Note:* the skeptic **confirmed** first-hand that ingestion walks `corpus/index` (no `index` in any exclusion list), the 772/522/25 tallies, the Chroma collection inventory, completeness of the literal-string grep, zero `.claude/` coupling, no `package.json` script, the `.gitignore` state, that `corpus-index-provider.ts` genuinely ignores its `indexPath`, that hooks are Aristotle-only, and the five `.backups` directories.\n\n### 11.E Memory-file corrections surfaced by the audit\n\n| Memory claim | Reality |\n|---|---|\n| \"ChromaDB collections metaphysics/new_media/rhetorical_ontology\" | **There is exactly ONE collection, `knowledge_chunks`.** Those are values of the per-chunk metadata field `collection`, filtered via a `where` clause (`run_ingest_phase2.py:192-193, :1094, :1742`; `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:90, :920`) |\n| \"QuotationFidelityValidator (70%+)\" | Stage threshold is **0.90** (`quotation-fidelity-stage.ts:60-61`); validator uses verbatim ≥0.95 / normalized ≥0.95 raw ≥0.80 / borderline ≥0.90 raw ≥0.75 |\n| \"QualityGauntlet (7 stages)\" | **10 default stages**, weights summing to ~1.20 then normalized (`quality-gauntlet.ts:574-589`). Code comments still say 7 |\n| \"compiled-index.json built by `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` NOT `god-learn compile`\" | **CORRECT and re-confirmed.** `god-learn compile` → `scripts/god_learn/god_learn.py:333-341` = Phase 1–3 ingest/audit/verify; `grep 'compiled-index'` on that file → no hits |\n| \"Secondary-literature clusters NOT registered, by design\" (`project-compiled-index-registration.md`) | **Policy reversed in practice between 2026-06-23 and 2026-07.** Boredom Secondary (61 nodes) and VR Pedagogy Secondary (60) are now the two largest contributors to `compiled-index.json`, enabled by the `cluster-ontology.md` fallback (`compile-corpus-index.py:1217-1224`). RDR2 Secondary and Phantasia Secondary remain unregistered — and, per C2, currently **unregisterable without an ontology-format rewrite** |\n| \"corpus/index FIRST, ChromaDB fallback\" (`feedback-corpus-index-first.md`) | **A human workflow rule only.** Zero code implements it; live order is inverted (§1.3) |\n| \"God-write: EMBEDDED PACK not corpus retrieval\" | **Verified in code** for the no-flag path (`write-pipeline-orchestrator.ts:3752-3756`) — **but** the documented `/god-write` invocation uses `--use-corpus` (`.claude/commands/god-write.md:27-33`), which under default v2 **does** inject index blocks (`:3532`). Pack-only mode requires dropping `--use-corpus` |\n\n### 11.F Items that remain UNVERIFIED (source truncation)\n\n1. The 11th `tension-edges.json` file's schema (10 of 11 enumerated).\n2. The full `SYSTEM-REVIEW-GAPS.md` item list (only B5, H1, H2, H7, H-12, O1, C-03 recovered via cross-references).\n3. MASTER-PLAN 7-phase item **Phase 7** status.\n4. The remainder of the release-manifest finding (S-2) and of the `getCompiledIndex` naming-collision finding.\n5. Three of the nine entries with no machine-readable source path.\n6. The 20+ vs 42 edge-CSV header-dialect count reconciliation.\n7. Whether the +0.10 canonical boost applied **after** the cross-encoder was ever evaluated in the rerank A/B harness (`scripts/test-rerank-wiring.ts`).\n8. Whether `RetrievalOptions.collections` was ever functional in a prior revision (not traced through git history).\n9. Whether `FacetedRetrieval` (ICP path) is intended to get reranking at all — ICP and the write pipeline currently use materially different retrieval quality.\n10. Whether the `Debate axis N:` entries in `canonicalTerms` are intentional or an extraction bug.",
